Example 17 1-(3,5-Di-0-benzyl-2,6-di-0-(p-toluenesulphonyl)-β-D-allofuranosyl)thymine (17). To a stirred solution of nucleoside 16 (0.60 g, 1.28 mmol) in dichloromethane (70 cm3) at 20 room temperature was added 4-Λ/,N-(dimethylamino)pyridine (0.63g, 5J2 mmol) and p-toluenesulphonyl chloride (0.73 g, 3.84 mmol). After stirring for 3 h, ice-cold H20 (50 cm3) was added and extraction was performed using dichloromethane (3 x 75cm3). The combined organic phase was dried (Na2S04) and evaporated to dryness under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography 25 using dichloromethane/methanol (99.5:0.5, v/v) as eluent to give nucleoside 17 as white solid material (0.71 g, 71 %) after evaporation of the solvents under reduced pressure. δH (CDCI3) 8.83 (1H, br s), 7.73-7J2 (18H, m), 6.58 (1H, d, J 1.2), 5.88 (1H, d, J 6.9), 5.0 (1H, m), 4.73-3.82 (9H, m), 2.40 (3H, s), 2.35 (3H, s),1.48 (3H, d, JO.9). 30 δc(CDCI3) 163.1, 149.8, 145.8, 145.2, 137.1, 137.0, 135.6, 132.4, 132.3, 130.0, 128.7, 128.5, 128.3, 128.1, 128.0, 127.8, 127.2, 111.4, 86.9, 83.1, 77.7, 75.3, 73.1, 72.5, 67.4, 21.7, 11.9. FAB-MS m/z 777 [M + H] + . Found (%) C, 60.6; H, 5.2; N, 3.5; 

